# Overview
#
# A fancy word stands in for a plainer one (`enhance` for `improve`, `as
# per` for `according to`). The fancy word adds length and no meaning,
# and a reader who does not know it must look it up. The fix writes the
# plain word, and the message names the fix for each word. Each word
# here also appears in plain human-written docs. The rule therefore sits
# at Optional, where a finding suggests a change rather than asking for
# one.
#
# Expression
#
# `additionally` counts only with a glued comma, and `moreover` and
# `furthermore` count without the comma. `as per` and `per` before
# `the`, `its`, `your`, or `their` stand in for `according to` (`per the
# setting`). `As such,` stands in for `so`, and it counts only with its
# comma.
#
# False Positives
#
# `enhanced` stays out, because it opens feature names (`Enhanced
# Networking`, `Security Enhanced Linux`). `additionally` needs its
# comma, because mid-sentence it modifies a verb (`the flag additionally
# checks the signature`). Neither `moreover` nor `furthermore` modifies
# a verb, so both count without the comma.
#
# `per` alone stays out, because it also names a rate (`requests per
# user`). `as such` needs its comma, because without one it names a role
# (`the value is treated as such`).
#
# Related Rules
#
# The Required ProseFancyWord holds `utilize` and `leverage`, whose
# plain word is always `use`. The Recommended ProseFancyWord holds the
# words that turn up far more in generated text than in docs a person
# wrote. Their plain word differs from word to word. The Optional
# ProseFancyWord holds the words that human-written docs also use.
#
# Measurement
#
# The rule hit 191 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 20 of 20 sampled
# hits stood in for a plainer word. `enhance` hit 40 lines of the
# corpus, and the opener `Additionally,` hit 63. `Moreover` and
# `furthermore` join `Additionally,` here, because the two hit 24 lines
# of the same corpus. `facilitate` sits here too, because it hit 20
# lines (`to facilitate testing`). `as per` and `per` before `the`,
# `its`, `your`, or `their` hit 19 lines, and `As such,` hit 25.
expr main [enhance, enhances, enhancing, (additionally,), moreover, furthermore, facilitate, facilitates, facilitated, facilitating, (as per), (per [the, its, your, their]), (as such,)]
let message "Fancy word. Write `improve` or `extend` for `enhance`, `according to` for `as per` or `per the`, and `so` for `as such`. State what the subject does instead of `facilitate`. Delete `additionally`, `moreover`, or `furthermore`, or write `also`."
let description "Flags `enhance`, `facilitate`, `as per`, `per the`, and the openers `additionally`, `moreover`, `furthermore`, and `as such`, which stand in for plainer words."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The enhancement label marks feature requests."
allows "The flag additionally checks the signature."
allows "The quota counts requests per user."
